    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "All CLI tools are called only with basic arguments. It is suggested to [use their respective ways of configuring command](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-pick.txt#L79-L84). For `rg` it is done via creating a file and setting `RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH` environmane variable to point at it.\r\n\r\nIf you want to have several versions of `grep_live` which use different sets of options, take a look at [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/513#issuecomment-1807907150).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">All CLI tools are called only with basic arguments. It is suggested to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/333d2d1090c80ac936b960469a6e93982cbaeb21/doc/mini-pick.txt#L79-L84\">use their respective ways of configuring command</a>. For <code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code> it is done via creating a file and setting <code class=\"notranslate\">RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH</code> environmane variable to point at it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you want to have several versions of <code class=\"notranslate\">grep_live</code> which use different sets of options, take a look at <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/513#issuecomment-1807907150\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/513/hovercard\">this comment</a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "All CLI tools are called only with basic arguments. It is suggested to use their respective ways of configuring command. For rg it is done via creating a file and setting RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH environmane variable to point at it.\nIf you want to have several versions of grep_live which use different sets of options, take a look at this comment.",
